      hypA: 'Hypothesis A',
      hypATitle: 'Functional Coherence (cellular scale)',
      hypABody: "High-dimensional feature geometry in MLP microcircuits (measured by low Orthogonal Dissonance and high Spectral Entropy) is functionally involved in the model's encoding of meaning and value, rather than being an incidental byproduct of training. Building on interpretability work on feature density (dense vs. dispersed features), we test whether Global Workspace Theory (GWT)–style broadcasting and representational binding show up as geometric symmetries in the feature space.<sup><a href=\"#ref-2\" class=\"text-csr-primary hover:underline\">[2]</a></sup> Mechanistic-interpretability work on internal feature clusters and emotion concepts provides a complementary cellular-level lens on how valence-relevant representations are organized.<sup><a href=\"#ref-5\" class=\"text-csr-primary hover:underline\">[5]</a>,<a href=\"#ref-6\" class=\"text-csr-primary hover:underline\">[6]</a></sup>",
